    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-43-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person attempts to obstruct, to prevent, to pervert or to defeat the course of justice in relation to a judicial power; and  (b) the judicial power is the judicial power of the Commonwealth. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@type": "xsd:decimal",
        "@value": "1.0000"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits attempting to obstruct or pervert justice.",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person attempts to obstruct, to prevent, to pervert or to defeat the course of justice in relation to a judicial power; and  (b) the judicial power is the judicial power of the Commonwealth. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years."
    },
